{% endif %}
{% if adbs_nets %}
    ├── gcp-odb-network-adbs/ # ODB Network, client subnet only (ADB-S)
{% endif %}
{% if wants_dedicated %}
    ├── gcp-exadata-infra/   # Exadata Infrastructure (hardware)
{% endif %}
{% if wants_dedicated and exascale %}
    ├── gcp-vm-cluster/      # ExaDB VM Cluster (compute)
{% endif %}
{% if exascale %}
    ├── gcp-exascale-vault/  # Exascale Database Storage Vault
    {{ '├──' if adbs else '└──' }} gcp-exascale-vm-cluster/ # Exascale VM Cluster
{% endif %}
{% if adbs %}
{% if wants_dedicated and not exascale %}
    ├── gcp-vm-cluster/      # ExaDB VM Cluster (compute)
{% endif %}
    └── gcp-autonomous-db/   # Autonomous AI Database Serverless
{% elif not exascale %}
    └── gcp-vm-cluster/      # ExaDB VM Cluster (compute)
{% endif %}
```
{% if exascale and not wants_dedicated %}

**Exascale only.** There is no Exadata Infrastructure to provision: the VM
clusters run on Oracle-managed Exascale infrastructure and keep their databases
in an Exascale Database Storage Vault. The ODB Networks keep their backup
subnet, which an Exascale VM Cluster needs.
{% elif not wants_dedicated %}

**Autonomous Serverless only.** Oracle runs the fleet, so this configuration has
no Exadata Infrastructure and no VM Cluster — and its ODB Networks build a client
subnet but no backup subnet, because an Autonomous Database never uses one.
{% endif %}

