## Important Notes

- **Deletion protection** is enabled by default on all resources. To destroy,
  set `deletion_protection = false` and apply before running `terraform destroy`.
- **Compute/storage counts** on Exadata Infra are ignored after initial creation
  (controlled by Oracle, not Terraform).
- **SSH public keys** on VM Clusters are also ignored after creation.
{% if adbs %}
- **Autonomous Database scaling fields are ignored after creation** —
  `compute_count`, storage size, version, edition, the auto-scaling flags and
  backup retention. Autonomous scaling rewrites these values in place, so
  without the guard every plan would propose shrinking the database back to its
  seed size. Editing them in `terraform.auto.tfvars` therefore produces no plan;
  to resize deliberately, comment the field out of the `lifecycle.ignore_changes`
  block in `modules/gcp-autonomous-db/main.tf`, apply, then restore it.
- **`gcp_adb_admin_passwords` has no default.** `terraform plan` fails until the
  environment variable above is exported.
{% endif %}
- This configuration expects a **pre-existing VPC network**. The network path is
  set in `gcp_odb_networks[*].network`.
